Resource requirements for evaluating this artifact
==================================================

All values below were measured on a clean clone of the public repository
using /usr/bin/time -v. They describe the reproduction path that evaluators
are asked to run. They do NOT describe the original data collection, which is
not part of the proposed evaluation (see "Not required" at the bottom).

Compute
-------
CPU            Any x86-64 or ARM64 processor. Single core is sufficient;
               the analyzers are not parallelized.
GPU            None.
Memory         Peak resident set size 430,768 kB (about 421 MB), reached by the
               cross-benchmark module, which loads the per-session records of
               both benchmarks. Per module: rq1 84 MB, rq2 302 MB, rq3 111 MB,
               cross-benchmark 421 MB. Provision at least 1 GB of RAM.
Disk           Working tree            62 MB
               Git history             114 MB (only if cloned with history)
               Python virtualenv      322 MB
               Total, worst case      about 500 MB.
Network        Required once, to clone the repository and to install the four
               Python packages. The reproduction itself makes no network
               calls, needs no API keys, and no proxy.

Time
----
Environment setup      about 30 s (uv venv + uv pip install)
Full reproduction       7.2 s measured wall clock for all four modules
Verification            under 1 s
Total                  well under 5 minutes including the clone.

Software
--------
OS             Linux x86-64 (tested). macOS and Windows Subsystem for Linux
               are expected to work; nothing in the reproduction path is
               platform specific.
Python         3.12 or newer. Verified on 3.13.9.
Packages       numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.9.2, pandas 2.2.3
               (pinned in artifact/requirements-repro.txt).
Other          bash. Optionally uv, which the install script uses when present
               and otherwise falls back to python3 -m venv and pip.
               No compilers, no paid software, no license servers, no GUI.

Not required for evaluation
---------------------------
The original measurement campaign ran between March 22 and April 13, 2026 and
consumed approximately 500 GPU-hours across six locally served agents on
NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell GPUs (96 GB VRAM each), plus paid OpenAI API
usage for the seventh agent. It also measured the live web, which has changed
since. That path is released for inspection and single-session demonstration
under artifact/pipeline/, and its prerequisites are documented in
artifact/INSTALL.md, but it is not reproducible in principle and is not part
of the proposed evaluation.
